/ContextArtifact in lingxi-kernel + lingxi-service wiring:\nsingle compile/render/observe source for model requests (system_prompt now\ncarries the compiled artifact render), context-observation endpoint, frozen\n24-segment registry with per-segment budgets and zh/en goldens.\n\nR06-A01/R06-A02 PASS under independent adversarial review (REVIEWER-R06-T01-R1,\nlocked toolchain 1.98.1): 42 new tests + R05 regression 21/21 + workspace\n1528 passed/0 failed + black-box e2e probe 15/15.\n\nNon-blocking findings F-01..F-06 registered as post-acceptance obligations in\ndocs/rust-tauri/R06/R06_PROGRESS.json."), "parents": Array [String("c9cca6020e0990016ee0d14af406766370849a7a")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("b174e3ff4"), "subject": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R06-T01 context compiler and short-prompt artifact")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1791443087), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("c9cca6020e0990016ee0d14af406766370849a7a"), "message": String("fix(rust-tauri): F54 semantic resurvey — 46 exclusive leaves reclassified 6 full/49 share/69 deferred, gate PASS\n\nReverts the false full_original_behavior claims from RR3 M-01: ~40 of the\n46 R04-exclusive leaves had mechanism-face cases (directory placeholder,\nconnector handshake, generation delta, permission grid, terminal echo)\npinned as if they proved product-semantics assertions (e.g. ast_grep\n'discoverable, NEVER callable' pinned for 'return match locations and\nsnippets'). New split after per-assertion audit: A=2, B=1 (write_stdin\nre-pin), C=3 (real production-entry proofs added: route-consistency MCP\nleg, describe generation conservation, search honest availability),\nD=40 (authoritative deferral: R00 execution_stage_ids multi-stage\nrevision via r00_t07_build_map.py generator chain — R07-T08/T09/T12\nand R08-T01/T02/T07 carry-over clauses pinned per leaf in laterShare;\nassertions byte-identical, SCOPE_DECISION_REQUIRED=0).\n\n- stage_maps/R04.json rebuilt via generator: 6 full + 49 share + 69\n  deferred (was 46/9/69); verify.rs validator semantics unchanged\n- r04_t08_tool_matrix.rs: MCP route-comparison leg + 2 new producer\n  cases; xtask mirror updated (58 cases)\n- 7 negative checks recorded (uncallable-as-full, echo-as-variable-\n  sharing, handshake-as-resource-read, assertion deletion, invented\n  stage, unowned deferral all rejected + positive control); 3 re-run\n  independently by reviewer\n- Formal gate verify-stage R04 (F54-CLOSEOUT-01/verify-R04):\n  overall=PASS, testedSha=def860a74+worktree, binding stable, 8\n  commands exit0, leaf table 55/0/69, 24/24 scenarios, 58 cases ok\n- Independent review REVIEWER-F54-R1: PASS, no mustFix (36 leaves\n  clause-level basis check, 6/6 full leaves source-read, 21 share\n  sampled, 3 negative checks re-run) — F54-REVIEW-01/\n- Ledgers updated: R00 dual ledgers (stage fields only, generator\n  chain), RR3_ISSUE_MATRIX F54 row, RR3_PROGRESS, R05_HANDOFF\n  M_F54 semantic_resurvey; R06_READY=true stands on honest split\n- Historical M-01/M-REVIEW-01 records preserved unmodified"), "parents": Array [String("def860a74abd174a2297a7adfbc8799d400aabea")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("c9cca6020"), "subject": String("fix(rust-tauri): F54 semantic resurvey — 46 exclusive leaves reclassified 6 full/49 share/69 deferred, gate PASS")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1791428258), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("def860a74abd174a2297a7adfbc8799d400aabea"), "message": String("chore(rust-tauri): RR3 localOnly archive closeout — 6,290 deleted / 61 binaries relocated, receipts committed\n\nPost-delivery hygiene per user approval:\n- ARCH-01: deleted 5,851 localOnly originals (769,208,829 B: build caches\n  3,442, isolated source copies 1,199, LOCAL_ONLY snapshot class 1,074,\n  runtime tickets/state 136), each with pre-deletion SHA256 verification\n  against the DELIVERY-FINAL-02 classification (5,912/5,912 gate pass);\n  relocated 61 LOCAL_BINARY originals (448,967,152 B) byte-preserving to\n  ../LingxiAgent-RR3-localonly-evidence/ with per-file destination SHA\n  checks; 39 RELOCATED-ARCH01 markers committed at affected parents.\n- ARCH-01-R2: 439 legacy snapshot remnants (R01-era, 69,088,347 B) exposed\n  by the nested .gitignore removal were registered (path/bytes/SHA256/mtime)\n  then deleted.\n- Boundary updates: 6,290 historically_removed + 61 relocated, receipts\n  referenced; tracked tree zero change (ls-files -s 64d610a9…, diff HEAD\n  empty); independent review PASS 7/7 (ARCH-REVIEW-01/REVIEW.md).\n- Disclosure: the 134,457,480-byte rlib was classified LOCAL_BUILD_CACHE\n  and deleted per the category rule; SHA ef146b51… dual-source verified;\n  substance-rebuildable from committed source + locked toolchain, not\n  byte-identical (adhoc re-sign).\n- Residual: 100 root-.gitignore-hidden files (.mimosa/pycache/reviews)\n  intentionally untouched, invisible in git status."), "parents": Array [String("b4b0094d37d4de2b1914d8c8de5e89cdf79312a6")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("def860a74"), "subject": String("chore(rust-tauri): RR3 localOnly archive closeout — 6,290 deleted / 61 binaries relocated, receipts committed")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1791418081), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("b4b0094d37d4de2b1914d8c8de5e89cdf79312a6"), "message": String("docs(rust-tauri): RR3 git delivery receipt — d1786a34f pushed, seal not advanced (R05 accepted, R06_READY=true)"), "parents": Array [String("d1786a34f3d3d37a399dc3a5d20f41799eaf99a4")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("b4b0094d3"), "subject": String("docs(rust-tauri): RR3 git delivery receipt — d1786a34f pushed, seal not advanced (R05 accepted, R06_READY=true)")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1791417210), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("d1786a34f3d3d37a399dc3a5d20f41799eaf99a4"), "message": String("fix(rust-tauri): R05 RR3 closeout — F42-F54 closed, FINAL-04 stage review PASS, R06_READY=true\n\nRound-3 (RR3) closeout of R05, per RR3 master prompt 2026-10-07 (inheriting\nRR1 2026-10-04 / RR2 2026-10-06 specs in full):\n\n- F42 (A): cross-layer candidate binding fixed for the whole R05→R04→R03→R02\n  chain — first formal main-tree run with candidateSourceBinding.stable=true\n  and ALL checkpoints stable on every layer (R05 7/7, R04 8/8, R03 15/15);\n  R02 real-OS-fd sink discovery with DIR-unit fencing and illegal-root\n  rejection (fail-closed on git query errors). Two review rounds.\n- F45 (B): N03 negative gate resolves the unique authority-table target and\n  count dynamically (24→23 exactly once, named red, byte-exact restore).\n- F27-RR3/I10 (C) + F46: full resource steady-state evidence (160 mixed\n  rounds, 54+61 sample points, 15 live workers, 45 steady, 20 recompute,\n  34 PID exits), measurement negative controls (fake-FD/TCP zero detected),\n  logging prune-before-open keeps the 3-file cap across restarts (old 6-run\n  red [1,2,3,4,4,4] → fixed [1,2,3,3,3,3] green).\n- F47/F48 (H): r02_t01 smoke guard INFO prerequisite + redaction preserves\n  real request_id correlation (49-byte ids unmasked, secrets still masked).\n- F49 (I): negative-gate reset covers kernel mutations; full restore honest.\n- F50 (J): default isolated copies get full Node dependency prep\n  (HEAD 38066 + Node 1277/64760), legacy BASE materialized via CoW.\n- F51/F52: 56 nested-.git fixture dirs + 1 symlink relocated out of the\n  main tree with byte-preserving receipts — candidate binder surface now\n  100% regular files (fail-closed contract untouched).\n- F53 (L): PTY snapshot race hardened (marker readiness barrier waits for\n  all observable echo copies); assertion semantics unchanged, detection\n  power proven by mutation red/green.\n- F54 (M): 46 R04-exclusive leaves reclassified full_original_behavior with\n  119 case pins from the real r04_tool_matrix case set; validator untouched.\n- G-REVIEW-03: default N01-N16 all fail-closed and named, controls green,\n  real shell exit=0 persisted; full R02 chain 20/20 + full E5/seal-family\n  GREEN (G01's seven failures all resolved).\n- FINAL-04 (fresh independent stage review): all six §5.3 commands exit 0;\n  verify-stage R05 overall=PASS on every layer; R05 18/18 scenarios +\n  130/130 leaves; R04 24/24 + 55/0/69; R03 17/17; failure list empty.\n  Six-tuple: offline_gate=PASS, independent_review=PASS,\n  stage_readiness=ACCEPTED_OFFLINE_SCOPE_WITH_REGISTERED_LIVE_DEFERRALS,\n  R06_READY=true (live BLOCKED_NOT_AUTHORIZED per original permission,\n  latest R10; Linux inherited, Windows not verified).\n- r00/ALF: four binary identities across FINAL-01..04; every LAN assertion\n  run passed from FINAL-01 on (6+ runs); no evidence any user firewall\n  action is required; per-instance observational attribute retained.\n- Storage blocker resolved by controller cargo clean (280.7GiB regenerable\n  cache) + partial RR2-era /tmp scratch recovery, receipts in TASK0.\n- Delivery: DELIVERY-FINAL-02 classification (29,158 include / 5,912\n  localOnly / 0 unknown) independently reviewed PASS; 163 CRLF originals\n  archived as raw blobs via hash-object --no-filters + update-index\n  (index blob SHA1 == raw expectation, 0 mismatches).\n\nEvery work package, repair round, acceptance, and the final stage review\nused a fresh empty-history agent. All historical FAILs preserved. Seal\n(VERIFIED_SOURCE_SHA=ab4f2281…) NOT advanced this round: desktop/cli\nnpm-side code changed since R01 without npm-chain verification evidence in\nthis round; advancement left to the authorized desktop verification round."), "parents": Array [String("b3ac0e6aeae8d7d530a6ab8657a5fa9ce4849f0b")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("d1786a34f"), "subject": String("fix(rust-tauri): R05 RR3 closeout — F42-F54 closed, FINAL-04 stage review PASS, R06_READY=true")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1791313335), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("b3ac0e6aeae8d7d530a6ab8657a5fa9ce4849f0b"), "message": String("docs(rust-tauri): RR2 handoff git receipt + ALF unblock path (commit e8c0672e5)"), "parents": Array [String("e8c0672e57851bc6b94d5a9149854c0b5fdb612a")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("b3ac0e6ae"), "subject": String("docs(rust-tauri): RR2 handoff git receipt + ALF unblock path (commit e8c0672e5)")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1791313195), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("e8c0672e57851bc6b94d5a9149854c0b5fdb612a"), "message": String("fix(rust-tauri): R05 RR2 closeout — 6 items closed + F44, stage review NOT_ACCEPTED on ALF env item only (R06_READY=false)\n\nRound-2 (RR2) closeout of R05, per RR2 master prompt 2026-10-06:\n\n- F41: R02 storage registry gains v6/v7 (names, SQL SHA256, provenance;\n  fingerprints cross-verified against real inspector receipts; v1-v5\n  preserved); S0 equality self-check (r02_registry_consistency.py) wired\n  into r02_t04_storage_tx.sh; 3 isolated mutations fail precisely.\n  Independent review PASS (A-R2/REVIEW-r1.md).\n- F42: r02_t08_legacy_entry_regression.sh run-output ownership rework —\n  process-tree fd sink discovery (fail-closed), DIR units fenced\n  (>=4 levels, no tracked content, dedication check, FILE fallback),\n  RUN_OUTPUT_ROOTS attestation with illegal-root rejection; bindings,\n  cmp, race detection, raw logs all preserved; .gitignore untouched.\n  Full standalone chain exit 0 (s5-full-5). Review PASS (B-R2/R2/REVIEW-r2.md).\n- F44 (new): spawnSync maxBuffer (64MB) in seal-trio tests + diff guard —\n  ENOBUFS crashes gone, registered seal classes parse again.\n  Classifier form-evolution for patch-too-large (>git MAX_APPLY_SIZE,\n  3.67GB patches) registered with strict shapes; note-quoting fix.\n- F34: permanent Anthropic unclosed-block leg (only content_block_stop\n  missing, stop_reason=tool_use) + positive control; mutation red/green\n  verified two ways; pins/cids 9->10 with xtask mirror. Review PASS.\n- F43: pid-file completeness barrier (r04_a09), real worker readiness\n  barrier + honest SIGTERM contract (f24); root cause: nonce purpose\n  never mapped (historical greens were false passes). Full workspace\n  green window achieved once (exit 0, 1476 passed, D-R2/REVIEW-r1.md).\n  Review PASS (b)(c).\n- F31: OAuth model listing non-OAuth rejection restored to 404 per\n  original R00 leaf; minimal-body, no existence oracle; deviation\n  registry superseded; other OAuth surfaces keep 409. Review PASS.\n- F40: three appended C-ID matrix rows closed with evidence; resource\n  records per 160 mixed-round baseline.\n- G: I01-I11 mapping all PASS (G-R2/I-MAPPING.md); N01-N16 + 6 new\n  counterexamples 16/16 + 6/6 in isolated copies (G-R2/NEG-GATE-RR2.md).\n\nStage review (FINAL-01, fresh reviewer, personally executed): fmt/clippy/\ncontracts/boundaries exit 0; r05_stage_suites 27+64 PASS; R02/R03/R04\nchains pass except the workspace cascade; 130 leaves/137 cases PASS;\nF27 resource series regenerated. Verdict NOT_ACCEPTED, R06_READY=false —\nsole blocker is R05-ENV-ALF-UNSIGNED-TEST-BINARY (macOS firewall blocks\nunsigned r00 test binary's non-loopback listener; needs user Allow, then\na FINAL-02 rerun). Six-field status in FINAL-01/STAGE_REVIEW.md.\n\nDocs: RR2 matrix/progress/handoff/brief; R05 report/ledger/handoff/\nblockers updated to READY_FOR_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW truth; orchestrator\nprogress current_head -> ad5ec4e98. Residue from an interrupted prior\nsession relocated out of the repo (backup dir beside the repo).\n\nNo commit of secrets (synthetic test keys only in run logs). Seal NOT\nadvanced (gates not fully green — advancing would be dishonest)."), "parents": Array [String("ad5ec4e9853a51ed929f1e2e077b97d41c951572")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("e8c0672e5"), "subject": String("fix(rust-tauri): R05 RR2 closeout — 6 items closed + F44, stage review NOT_ACCEPTED on ALF env item only (R06_READY=false)")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1791247114), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("ad5ec4e9853a51ed929f1e2e077b97d41c951572"), "message": String("fix(rust-tauri): R05 RR1 adversarial repair — F01–F28 closed, stage review NOT_ACCEPTED (R06_READY=false)\n\nRound-1 repair of the R05 adversarial review (evidence pack\nartifacts/rust-tauri/R05/RR1/INPUT-adversarial-2026-10-04, audited HEAD d80737b6):\n\n- F01/F02 per-model capability declarations + config-generation snapshot routing\n- F03–F05 credential handle epoch, OAuth backend closed loop (six R00 leaves),\n  sanitize-before-truncate diagnostics (new credentials/login.rs)\n- F06–F10 protocol replay: Anthropic thinking signatures, Google functionCall\n  thought signatures + parallel result grouping, DeepSeek reasoning_content,\n  opaque provenance binding, Responses/Codex ordering\n- F11–F13 whole-batch admission before side effects (batch_admission.rs),\n  trustworthy termination, single normalization source for live/final/history\n- F14–F16 unified network policy (network.rs), egress DNS-candidate validation,\n  absolute deadlines across error-body/queue/refresh/download waits\n- F17–F20 canonical-scope attachment reads, media task dual identity,\n  cancel fences through poll/download/register, macOS system speech under\n  unified permit/deadline supervision (real /usr/bin/say evidence)\n- F21–F23 per-attempt usage ledger, strict usage parsing + redacted invalid\n  details, Gemini thoughts/candidates accounting\n- F24–F28 production four-tool + worker wiring, exclusive-leaf share matrix,\n  C-ID identity gates, resource sampling with raw time series, report consistency\n- F29–F40 new findings registered and closed during repair (37/40\n  independent-pass); RR1 ledger under docs/rust-tauri/R05/repair-current/\n\nStage status: offline suites pass on macOS arm64 (r05_stage_suites 91 runs,\n130/130 leaves, fmt/clippy/contracts/boundaries exit 0), but the independent\nstage reviewer re-ran verify-stage R05 → NOT_ACCEPTED, R06_READY=false.\nOpen: F31 (leaf 404→409 deviation registration), F34 (Anthropic unclosed-block\npermanent test leg), F40 (ledger rows T05-C11B/C13, T06-C11B), F41 (R02 storage\nregistry missing v6/v7), F42 (.gitignore *.log whitelist × r02_t08 E0 mirror\nbinding), F43 (rust_test_workspace full-green window). See RR1_FINAL_REPORT.md."), "parents": Array [String("d80737b6cb9186c8a18c0f35923aac00249d45c3")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("ad5ec4e98"), "subject": String("fix(rust-tauri): R05 RR1 adversarial repair — F01–F28 closed, stage review NOT_ACCEPTED (R06_READY=false)")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1791089606), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("d80737b6cb9186c8a18c0f35923aac00249d45c3"), "message": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R05 T01-T08 model gateway, protocol adapters and full closed loop\n\n- T01: unified ModelGateway + typed model exchange contract\n  (model_exchange), provider registry, scope/provider/callsite matrices,\n  config-consumed bootstrap wiring, binary plane tests\n- T02: CredentialService per-provider coordinated refresh (flight merge,\n  atomic persistence, generation fence, revocation), oauth flows, redaction\n  boundaries, CREDENTIAL_FLOW_MATRIX\n- T03: real protocol adapters (anthropic-messages, google-generative-ai,\n  openai-responses, openai-codex-responses) with desensitized goldens,\n  call-id mapping, mixed content and opaque state round-trips\n- T04: production streaming switch, StreamDecoder + normalized event\n  bridge, bounded buffers, partial/stop-reason semantics, property tests\n- T05: egress guard, staged timeouts, budgeted retry classification,\n  cancel propagation across every wait class, compat goldens\n- T06: operations dialect (image/vision/embedding/speech/media), egress\n  SSRF legs, worker async model bridge on real subprocess RPC (permit=1\n  nesting, per-invocation budgets), WORKER_MODEL_BOUNDARY\n- T07: usage families per protocol (running-total vs delta), ModelCall\n  causality, persistence tx-before-publish, MODEL_USAGE_SEMANTICS\n- T08: stage_maps/R05.json + real producers, 16 appendix-C negative\n  injections on isolated copies, real-binary closed loop (nonce\n  double-run, restart re-read), R04/R03/R02 regression chains, full stage\n  docs (R05_REPORT/R05_HANDOFF/R05_TEST_MAP/NEGATIVE_GATE_REPORT/LIVE/\n  PERF/BLOCKERS)\n\nVerification: five gates (fmt/clippy -D warnings/test --workspace --locked/\ncheck-contracts/check-boundaries) green on the terminal tree; verify-stage\nR05 overall PASS (artifacts/rust-tauri/R05/FINAL-WFR2-1/verify-R05; executor\nattempts archived under T08-E01). Independent review: T06 and T07 closed\nafter mustFix repair rounds (REVIEW-T06, REVIEW-T07), T08 stage review PASS\nfirst round (REVIEW-T08, R05_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md, offline scope).\n\nLIVE provider verification BLOCKED_NOT_AUTHORIZED (registered, R10 at\nlatest); Windows/Linux platform items per prior ledger; no commit/push\nduring the run (authorization received afterwards).\n\ngitignore: exclude reviewer probe cargo target dirs; re-include rust-tauri\nevidence logs per R00-R04 convention."), "parents": Array [String("c549ff654508ab951e2cf39cf9d309fc9c6b8656")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("d80737b6c"), "subject": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R05 T01-T08 model gateway, protocol adapters and full closed loop")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790895691), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("c549ff654508ab951e2cf39cf9d309fc9c6b8656"), "message": String("docs(rust-tauri): re-accept R04 after RR1 adversarial repair (stage review PASS)\n\nSTAGE-REVIEWER-R04-RR1 (fresh, no participation in any repair round):\nSTAGE_VERDICT PASS on final candidate 629e15b85.\n\n- five counterexamples independently re-verified old-red/new-green\n  against the adversarial-review baseline 773d5a696 (refused command\n  really executed / detached pump mutated settled collector / invented\n  exit 137 / triple-delivered mixed chunk / lost-HEAD truncated=false\n  + capped spill claimed Full)\n- original gate re-run green (24 scenarios incl. 5 new RR1 REQUIRED,\n  124 leaves, embedded R03 17/17, RR1 producer 63 tests / 22 C-IDs);\n  negative gates 9/9 legacy + 4/4 RR1; standalone verify-stage R03\n  PASS with R02 chains 7/7\n- seven corrected acceptance bases recorded (registry-full vs\n  PreparedRegistryFull, common-not-rare trigger, timeout!=abort,\n  running-record!=not-reaped, CleanupTimedOut!=exit137, chunk seq !=\n  intra-chunk consumption, tail-window-not-truncated != complete);\n  historical reports preserved, t05-obs2-registryfull-tail deferred\n  registration closed by G01 with history kept\n- ledger receipts completed (G01-G05 commits pushed & remote-\n  confirmed), handoff gains reaccepted_after_rr1_adversarial_repair,\n  stage report R04_RR1_STAGE_REVIEW.md and evidence archived\n\nR04 RE-ACCEPTED AFTER ADVERSARIAL REPAIR. No R05 executor; stage\nstops here per authorization."), "parents": Array [String("629e15b85cf54ff20673b24150cc00e4e4366f61")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("c549ff654"), "subject": String("docs(rust-tauri): re-accept R04 after RR1 adversarial repair (stage review PASS)")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790890150), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("629e15b85cf54ff20673b24150cc00e4e4366f61"), "message": String("test(rust-tauri): R04 RR1 G05 — register repair scenarios in the R04 stage gate\n\nWire the five RR1 repair findings into the formal R04 gate:\n\n- stage map 19 -> 24 REQUIRED scenarios (R04-RR1-F01..F05) with a new\n  r04_rr1_repair_suites command; producer script pins 63 named tests\n  (6 integration suites + 26 exact lib tests) mapped to the 22 on-map\n  C-IDs; filter-zero, count drift, renames, missing C-IDs and orphan\n  executions all fail closed by name\n- xtask gains three pin tests (scenario registry + total 24, pin-table\n  mirror, C-ID coverage/count/no-double-attribution)\n- original 16 A-IDs, SUP obligations and the 124-leaf structure\n  untouched (55 share + 69 deferred); generator idempotence verified\n  twice byte-identical; R04_TEST_MAP gains the RR1 entries\n- full gate on the final tree: fmt/clippy/workspace (954 passed)/\n  check-contracts/check-boundaries exit 0; verify-stage R04 overall\n  PASS (8/8 commands, 24/24 scenarios, embedded R03 regression 17/17,\n  RR1 producer 32 runs green, stable binding); standalone verify-stage\n  R03 overall PASS (R02 targeted chains 7/7)\n- negative gates: legacy 9-case battery 9/9 fail-closed (C03b\n  completed by a faithful continuation runner after an external\n  SIGKILL); new RR1 battery 4/4 (delete F03 scenario -> pin test red\n  AND full verify-stage exit 1; pin 9->8 tamper; dropped C05 cid line)\n- first verify-stage attempt archived: legacy matrix case\n  terminal-snapshot-current-transcript flaked under load (isolated\n  rerun green in 0.21s, all subsequent legs green)\n\nREADY_FOR_REVIEW. Evidence: artifacts/rust-tauri/R04/RR1-G05-E01/"), "parents": Array [String("1285c3bf66ca251fe64956becd4aab44a6f3ef4d")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("629e15b85"), "subject": String("test(rust-tauri): R04 RR1 G05 — register repair scenarios in the R04 stage gate")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790870496), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("1285c3bf66ca251fe64956becd4aab44a6f3ef4d"), "message": String("fix(rust-tauri): R04 RR1 G04 repair — exact-once PTY consumption and honest output completeness\n\nR04-RR1-F04: TranscriptCore's cursor advanced only across fully\nconsumed chunks, so a mixed chunk ([a] + half of a multibyte char)\nre-delivered its already-returned prefix on the next poll and the\npending incomplete tail was counted as dropped.\n\nR04-RR1-F05: completeness was judged only against the rolling tail\nwindow (truncated = head_tail.truncated), so a lost prefix stayed\nunreported when the return budget exceeded the window, and capped or\nfailed spill files were still claimed as \"Full output\".\n\n- TranscriptCore: per-chunk consumed byte offset — every byte is\n  consumed at most once; pending-incomplete, ring-evicted (real loss),\n  replaced-invalid and result-truncation are reported as distinct\n  facts; decode_prefix_utf8 rewritten iteratively and aligned with\n  from_utf8_lossy maximal-subpart semantics (illegal byte followed by\n  an incomplete tail stays pending)\n- CollectorCore: true head window alongside the tail window (memory\n  bound 2x100KiB per process); OutputSnapshot exposes head and\n  lost_middle_bytes; SpillInfo separates failed from capped\n- exectools: assemble_retained_output with char-boundary-safe head/tail\n  fallback for single overlong lines; truncated = head_tail.truncated\n  || evicted > 0 (a legal budget cannot hide lost content); full-output\n  and transcript claims are four-state explicit (Full only for\n  byte-complete files); failed spill yields no ResourceRef;\n  run_write_stdin reports dropped/pending/replaced as separate lines\n- three new integration suites + fixed-seed property tests with\n  minimal-failure shrinker; legacy split-chunk control tests preserved\n\nIndependent review R1 PASS (reviewer-own baseline red: joined\n\"aaa日\" triple delivery and lost-HEAD truncated=false; candidate\ngreen; memory-bound identity asserted on real records; 72 fresh-seed\nproperty sequences). Evidence: artifacts/rust-tauri/R04/RR1-G04-E01/,\nRR1-G04-R1/"), "parents": Array [String("614fab1afa1ed2c45ebfe41045df4db339c4f9b5")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("1285c3bf6"), "subject": String("fix(rust-tauri): R04 RR1 G04 repair — exact-once PTY consumption and honest output completeness")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790865204), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("614fab1afa1ed2c45ebfe41045df4db339c4f9b5"), "message": String("fix(rust-tauri): R04 RR1 G03 repair — stop-unconfirmed honesty across exec/PTY/run chains\n\nR04-RR1-F03: unconfirmed cleanup was converted into fabricated exits —\ntimeout receipts fell back to ExitFact::Signal(9), CleanupTimedOut\nmapped to Signal(9)/Code(-1), write_stdin reported Exited{137}, and\nterminal_facts upgraded concurrent/duplicate terminations to a\nconfirmed Signal(9) with no observation behind it.\n\n- ToolRunStatus gains StopUnconfirmed{handle, detail}; ToolSuccess\n  status boxed (clippy large-err boundary)\n- ExitFact::Unobserved + observed_status_code() -> Option<i64>: exit\n  137 only from a real wait/trusted receipt; wait errors are\n  observation failures, never a fabricated -1/137\n- terminal_facts returns None for terminal-without-fact;\n  await_termination no longer upgrades unconfirmed terminations\n  (audited as termination_unconfirmed_echo); finalize_exit keeps the\n  first cause across the unconfirmed window\n- run_exec_command/run_write_stdin map receipts honestly: text and\n  structured status agree, unconfirmed keeps the original handle\n  queryable, normal 0 / nonzero / genuinely observed SIGKILL stay\n  exact (no blanket-Unknown downgrade)\n- runs.rs journal learns the StopUnconfirmed arm; R03 Cancelled and\n  Unknown semantics untouched\n- verification-only ReapFaultPoint injection (zero product callers);\n  4 existing suites adapted without weakening assertions; new suite\n  r04_rr1_f03_stop_honesty.rs (7 integration + 2 unit cases)\n\nIndependent review R1 PASS (reviewer-own baseline red 4/4 for the\nfabricated-137 family, candidate 6/6 green; control group proves no\nnonzero-to-Unknown downgrade; workspace 925/0). Evidence:\nartifacts/rust-tauri/R04/RR1-G03-E01/, RR1-G03-R1/"), "parents": Array [String("da15c4bd90a0bb8e27fa4a3fb0bca0ba7268cd82")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("614fab1af"), "subject": String("fix(rust-tauri): R04 RR1 G03 repair — stop-unconfirmed honesty across exec/PTY/run chains")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790860036), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("da15c4bd90a0bb8e27fa4a3fb0bca0ba7268cd82"), "message": String("fix(rust-tauri): R04 RR1 G02 repair — pump ownership, reap race and honest reclamation\n\nR04-RR1-F02: the reaper dropped stdout/stderr pump JoinHandles on\ngrace timeout (tokio detach, not abort), marked reclaimed=true\nunconditionally, and could still killpg on a stale pgid after the\ndirect child was reaped.\n\n- drain_output_tasks: keep pump JoinHandles; on grace expiry abort\n  and join within a second bounded budget; audited dispositions\n  (finished/panicked/closed_after_abort/end_unconfirmed); reclaimed\n  and drained_stdio now derive from real observation only\n- publish child_reaped right after wait() resolves, before the drain\n  grace; mark_terminating and the Drop fallback prove ownership at\n  send time (child_reaped == false + live getpgid re-check) and skip\n  with audit when unprovable — no signals on stale identities\n- verify_group now admits fast-exit children already reaped by tokio\n  (getpgid ESRCH) instead of a false EXEC_SPAWN_FAILED; live foreign\n  pgids still rejected\n- observation seams for verification only (task/pump counters,\n  exhaustive signal log, fault injection) — zero product callers\n- new suite r04_rr1_f02_reaper_cleanup.rs (11 cases) + strengthened\n  adversarial_parent_exit test (original assertions preserved)\n\nIndependent review R1 PASS (baseline red re-verified: settled\ncollector mutated post-terminal and fd leak; A09 legal control still\nkills the managed tree exactly once). Evidence:\nartifacts/rust-tauri/R04/RR1-G02-E01/, RR1-G02-R1/"), "parents": Array [String("1692d2314d381ac8da4aead6d2561878a5bb415b")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("da15c4bd9"), "subject": String("fix(rust-tauri): R04 RR1 G02 repair — pump ownership, reap race and honest reclamation")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790850694), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("1692d2314d381ac8da4aead6d2561878a5bb415b"), "message": String("fix(rust-tauri): R04 RR1 G01 repair — atomic capacity reservation before dispatch\n\nR04-RR1-F01: spawn paths checked live_cap only after OS spawn\n(kill_on_drop(false)), so a RegistryFull refusal left an unsupervised,\nalready-dispatched process with no handle for cancel/shutdown.\n\n- reserve_live_slot: atomic check-and-increment under the state lock,\n  before any OS resource creation (one-shot: pre-spawn; PTY: pre-open)\n- LiveSlot RAII guard: commit-on-success transfers release duty to the\n  record settle path; Drop returns the slot exactly once on every\n  failure path; rollbacks after dispatch kill+reap and close owned fds\n  while the error keeps the dispatch fact (with pid)\n- EXEC_PROCESS_REGISTRY_FULL separated from EXEC_SPAWN_FAILED and the\n  gateway PreparedRegistryFull vocabulary\n- new suite rust/crates/lingxi-service/tests/r04_t05_registry_capacity.rs\n  (9 cases, real gateway + real supervisor): C01 zero-dispatch refusal,\n  C02 barrier races (one-shot/PTY/mixed), C03 post-dispatch fault\n  compensation, C04 multi-round reuse; baseline red repro preserved\n\nIndependent review R1 PASS (old-red/new-green re-verified on baseline\nworktree; same-family regressions green). Evidence:\nartifacts/rust-tauri/R04/RR1-G01-E01/, RR1-G01-R1/"), "parents": Array [String("773d5a6968b87650cd135cc5684707f81d1acda0")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("1692d2314"), "subject": String("fix(rust-tauri): R04 RR1 G01 repair — atomic capacity reservation before dispatch")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790834747), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("773d5a6968b87650cd135cc5684707f81d1acda0"), "message": String("docs(rust-tauri): accept R04 after independent stage review (stage review R1 PASS)\n\nSTAGE-REVIEWER-R04-R01 (fresh agent, never part of any R04 execution,\nrepair or task review) independently re-ran on candidate 0c67b6fc7:\n- full R04 gate at a fresh evidence root: exit 0, 7/7 commands, 19/19\n  scenarios, 124 leaves = 55 pass + 69 deferred, candidateSourceBinding\n  stable, testedShaAtEnd = HEAD = origin\n- embedded full R03 gate PASS (15/15 commands, 17/17 scenarios)\n- six combination-chain probes (~1500 lines, path-dep on frozen candidate)\n  6/6: cross-entry consistency, full-args/approval-binding/generation\n  invalidation, ask-tier structured refusal + read_only/operate controls,\n  real read-edit-read conflicts + symlink + ghost-artifact refusal, real\n  3-generation process-tree cancel + sentinel + PTY, worker/MCP lost-receipt\n  Unknown + reconnect no-replay + R03 dedup counterexamples\n- RR2 acceptance chain ancestry verified; 8-task commit->review mapping\n  complete (T01/T02 include genuine FAIL->repair->R2-PASS history);\n  production defaults not silently switched; 69 deferred leaves and\n  platform deferrals preserved; platform matrix matches measured evidence\n\nNo blocking findings; 5 non-blocking observations registered in the report.\nAll historical FAIL records retained. Acceptance record references candidate\ncommit only (no self-SHA); this commit's SHA recorded via remote receipt."), "parents": Array [String("0c67b6fc749ac5c21d0514e3076b0ed2058cd7c4")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("773d5a696"), "subject": String("docs(rust-tauri): accept R04 after independent stage review (stage review R1 PASS)")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790831711), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("0c67b6fc749ac5c21d0514e3076b0ed2058cd7c4"), "message": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R04-T08 tool results, artifact verification and full matrix gate\n\n- artifactverify: dual-layer artifact verification (claimed-artifact within\n  grant + existence + regular-file + content contract, 64KiB bounded) and\n  gateway registration audit; audit_success_artifacts runs after dispatch,\n  before SUCCESS is booked — ghost/invalid references flip to explicit\n  Failed with honest three-part facts (dispatched / side effects possible /\n  nothing registered as delivered)\n- workerrpc: claimed-files converge to single authoritative verification;\n  fixture gains A15 adversarial modes (out-of-grant/self-deleting/dir-swap/\n  contract-violating)\n- T07 F1 closed: unique_dir per-process counter suffix (reproduced 3/8\n  collision, 15-run stability, reviewer 3 runs); T04 OBS-1 closed: edit\n  duplicate counting aligned to legacy fuzzy count space (edit-diff.js)\n- R04 stage gate: stage_maps/R04.json (19 scenarios = 16 A-IDs + SUP-01/03/05;\n  124 R00 leaves = 55 share-satisfied with assertion contracts + 69 deferred)\n  with real generator (idempotent), STAGE_MAPS + runner_identity registration;\n  verify-stage R04 exit 0 (7/7 commands, nested full verify-stage R03 PASS);\n  negative battery 9/9 (unknown stage/empty set/deleted leaf/deleted command/\n  missing SUP/zero-match filter/stale evidence/drift all non-zero with named\n  gaps); E02 fixed E01 stage-map defects (3 mispinned expects, 4 standard\n  commands silently skipped -> bound via R04-A15 refs)\n- acceptance: R04-A15/A16 PASS via independent reviewer R1 (first-round PASS);\n  workspace 888 passed / 0 failed; full matrix 56 pinned cases actual==expect\n- deliverables: R04_REPORT.md, R04_HANDOFF.json (R05-facing, no self SHA),\n  R04_ACCEPTANCE_LEDGER.json; N1/N2 factual corrections per R1 review\n- evidence: artifacts/rust-tauri/R04/T08-E01 + T08-R1-REVIEWER"), "parents": Array [String("ded3467bfe385a876b1316b86a7fbaf0a0ccfecf")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("0c67b6fc7"), "subject": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R04-T08 tool results, artifact verification and full matrix gate")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790805239), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("ded3467bfe385a876b1316b86a7fbaf0a0ccfecf"), "message": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R04-T07 MCP adapter and plugin worker RPC\n\n- mcpbridge: rmcp 3.4.1 (locked, D-06 feature set) real initialize/version\n  negotiation/paginated tools-list (page+tool double caps)/call/disconnect-\n  reconnect with exactly-one refresh handshake; tool:mcp:{server}:{tool}\n  identity, listing changes bump registry generation (old prepared handles\n  rejected at execute); untrusted annotations/remote URIs/session ids never\n  become local credentials; oversized output and schema-violating structured\n  results handled by contract; HTTP/SSE transports Unsupported-loud (locked\n  scope)\n- workerrpc: minimal single-op RPC (CSPRNG id, deadline, permits, size caps,\n  bounded mid-read line cap), concurrency semaphore + process-group kill,\n  host callback port (Unconfigured model capability = honest refusal, never\n  key hunting), claimed-files re-verification; workers never see provider\n  key store or whole home\n- integration via T02 gateway + T03 permission tiers; ToolOrigin mcp/plugin\n  per T01; E02 audited E01 interruption and fixed real defects by root cause\n  (pagination dead-loop, unbounded read_line, 6 assertion-contract\n  contradictions) with history preserved\n- acceptance: R04-A13/A14 PASS via independent reviewer R1 (first-round PASS,\n  3 fresh synthetic-server variants, marker-file zero-spawn proof); workspace\n  867 passed; R03 regression green; Cargo.lock gains single rmcp edge only\n- F1 registered for T08: T07 test unique_dir per-process counter suffix\n- evidence: artifacts/rust-tauri/R04/T07-E02; reports under docs/rust-tauri/R04"), "parents": Array [String("26251dc928209d460b77b4ad2042f8056a53e88a")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("ded3467bf"), "subject": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R04-T07 MCP adapter and plugin worker RPC")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790796539), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("26251dc928209d460b77b4ad2042f8056a53e88a"), "message": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R04-T06 cross-platform sandbox with escape protection\n\n- sandbox.rs: SandboxPolicy::derive (policy.ts port, 12 branches verbatim),\n  SandboxPort + frozen SandboxCapabilities matrix, Seatbelt backend\n  (deny-after-allow profile with realpath embedding, -p inline eliminating\n  legacy temp-profile TOCTOU, profile_literal rejecting quote/backslash/NUL\n  — closes legacy quote-injection escape independently confirmed exploitable\n  by reviewer S6 probe), bwrap backend, Unsupported backend (always refuse);\n  helper trust: pinned absolute path + root ownership + no group/world write\n  + basename match, construct-time + per-wrap double fail-closed\n- exectools: sandbox injection point — one-shot isolation path intersects\n  T04 cwd authorization, T05 env whitelist and T06 wrapping (no fallback\n  bypass); honest sandboxed annotation only when actually wrapped; tty keeps\n  legacy semantics (no OS sandbox) and never lies\n- platform matrix v2 frozen: macos-arm64 machine-verified; macos-x64 same\n  source not machine-verified; windows backend refuses (restricted-token\n  deferred per R03-WINDOWS-R09-R10); linux bwrap source-level not\n  machine-verified\n- acceptance: R04-A11/A12 PASS via independent reviewer R1 (first-round PASS,\n  29-leg cargo probes + shell-level probes, sentinel bytes unchanged,\n  injection variants rejected with zero side effects); workspace 840 passed;\n  R03 regression green; zero new crates, Cargo.lock unchanged\n- evidence: artifacts/rust-tauri/R04/T06-E01; reports under docs/rust-tauri/R04"), "parents": Array [String("84e6499fe0144b178bce827dde098b00af042a61")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("26251dc92"), "subject": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R04-T06 cross-platform sandbox with escape protection")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790791176), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("84e6499fe0144b178bce827dde098b00af042a61"), "message": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R04-T05 process supervisor, exec tools and PTY\n\n- procsupervisor: real ProcessSupervisor — setsid process groups with getpgid\n  post-verification, CSPRNG handles, bounded terminate chain (atomic mark ->\n  killpg SIGKILL -> bounded exit wait (5s default, honest CleanupTimedOut) ->\n  reaper with 250ms stdio grace), terminate_detached so future-drop never\n  loses ownership (kill_on_drop explicitly off), persistent-terminal lifetime\n  registry + shutdown_all freeze policy, libc-native PTY (O_NONBLOCK master,\n  TIOCSCTTY, TIOCSWINSZ), triple-bounded output with UTF-8 byte-cursor\n  delivery, non-Unix spawn fail-closed\n- exectools: native exec_command (argv/shell dual form, SAFE_ENV_PASSTHROUGH\n  explicit env whitelist — server secrets never inherited wholesale, bounded\n  timeout via supervisor chain, head/tail truncation + spill ResourceRef,\n  tty=true returns Running{handle}, never fake completion) and write_stdin\n  (format/record/terminal triple check, cross-principal NOT_OWNED refusal)\n- gateway integration via T02 net + T03 approval face; cwd scope reuses T04\n  ResourceAccess (symlink cwd adjudicated on real target)\n- acceptance: R04-A09/A10 PASS via independent reviewer R1 (first-round PASS;\n  4-PID tree ESRCH-verified with sentinel alive, future-drop path, PTY\n  resize/interrupt/exit chain); workspace 823 passed; R03 regression green\n- zero new crates; Cargo.lock unchanged; registered observations: stdio grace\n  delta vs legacy, RegistryFull orphan rare path, PTY master partial-reclaim\n- evidence: artifacts/rust-tauri/R04/T05-E01; reports under docs/rust-tauri/R04"), "parents": Array [String("80b4edbf5c0aed9f80d7655447a01afd4d087b1d")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("84e6499fe"), "subject": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R04-T05 process supervisor, exec tools and PTY")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790785958), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("80b4edbf5c0aed9f80d7655447a01afd4d087b1d"), "message": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R04-T04 native file tools with resource authorization\n\n- resourceaccess: ResourceAccess/ResourceOp/ResourceScope — real-target\n  symlink resolution (missing tail via nearest existing ancestor), canonical\n  component-wise root matching (no string-prefix), per-(principal,session)\n  read/write grant roots with revocation; windows reparse cfg-gated\n- filetools: native read (range/paging/truncation/binary-honest metadata/\n  duplicate-read stub), write (stale-since-read conflict, existence-verified\n  ResourceRef), edit (exact match + legacy fuzzy layer, CRLF/BOM preserved,\n  legacy error vocabulary); atomic same-dir O_EXCL temp + fsync + (dev,ino,\n  mtime,size) pre-rename identity re-verification + renameat + dir fsync;\n  Unix O_NOFOLLOW component walk with bounded churn re-authorization;\n  FileChangeLog checkpoint/rewind interface (failed writes record nothing)\n- gateway: ResourceExtractor normalization before policy/approval, resource\n  re-derivation before dispatch; approval records bind canonical resource\n  scopes; T03 OBS-1 real alias-resolution leg closed\n- acceptance: R04-A07/A08 PASS via independent reviewer R1 (first-round PASS,\n  15-test probe crate; legacy dangling-symlink escape independently\n  confirmed closed); workspace 804 passed / 0 failed; R03 regression green\n- registered observations: edit fuzzy-layer duplicate-count divergence from\n  legacy (T08 full-matrix review), post-rename stat narrow-window gap\n- evidence: artifacts/rust-tauri/R04/T04-E01; reports under docs/rust-tauri/R04"), "parents": Array [String("c72e0fa0226e685a92d5fbc1c7873db1de591d92")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("80b4edbf5"), "subject": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R04-T04 native file tools with resource authorization")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790780274), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("c72e0fa0226e685a92d5fbc1c7873db1de591d92"), "message": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R04-T03 approval lifecycle, revocation and read-only modes\n\n- approval_service: ApprovalService dual surface — ToolPolicyPort adjudication\n  (operate/ask/read_only user matrix + subagent {tier,parent_mode} matrix) and\n  ApprovalGate waiting surface (CSPRNG id, AbortOnDrop, bounded rings);\n  authenticated minimal interaction (ownership-checked pending_of/answer);\n  session-level preauthorization with atomic compare-and-decrement\n- SUP-01 (R03-T06-O1) CLOSED: parent-ask subagent write requests get\n  structured TOOL_APPROVAL_UNAVAILABLE (deny_on_prompt, allowHumanApproval\n  false), never folded into Operate; neighbors protected (ask+read allowed,\n  operate+write executes, read_only escalation denied pre/post dispatch,\n  explicit read decay preserved per T02 F01 fix)\n- approvals bind canonical args digest / target / principal / run /\n  generation / TTL / use count; cancel-beats-late-approval, timeout\n  determinism, restart ticket invalidation, concurrent single-spend (40x4)\n- T02 O05 closed: policy surface is sole source of approval need (pinned)\n- acceptance: R04-A05/A06 PASS via independent reviewer R1 (first-round PASS);\n  R03 regression green; workspace 788 passed / 0 failed\n- evidence: artifacts/rust-tauri/R04/T03-E01; reports under docs/rust-tauri/R04"), "parents": Array [String("39168bfb0dc5592c0d6e16d7c529bee74f2d30a4")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("c72e0fa02"), "subject": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R04-T03 approval lifecycle, revocation and read-only modes")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790776038), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("39168bfb0dc5592c0d6e16d7c529bee74f2d30a4"), "message": String("fix(rust-tauri): R04-T02 include toolcatalog origin field missed in 1a1602c33\n\nFollow-up commit within R04-T02 scope: PreparedToolCall.origin (server-side\nregistry manifest origin for delegation-family first-party routing, F01\nsame-root-cause closure) was part of the reviewed candidate (diff digest\n58b118cc0430c921) but was not staged with 1a1602c33 — that tree does not\ncompile. Append-only fix, no history rewrite. All other files unchanged."), "parents": Array [String("1a1602c3337be7f86e03ba510f9695ac9cafc8e8")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("39168bfb0"), "subject": String("fix(rust-tauri): R04-T02 include toolcatalog origin field missed in 1a1602c33")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790775875), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("1a1602c3337be7f86e03ba510f9695ac9cafc8e8"), "message": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R04-T02 route invocations through unified gateway\n\n- lingxi-service toolgateway: ToolInvocationGateway + PreparedInvocation\n  (CSPRNG handle, server-bound args/identity/principal/run/generation/TTL,\n  lock-scoped atomic redeem + registry revalidation), InvocationRequest via\n  from_trusted_entry only, FailClosedPolicy (unconfigured -> Execute-class\n  needs approval, never auto-Full; NeedsApproval w/o approval surface ->\n  TOOL_APPROVAL_UNAVAILABLE, zero dispatch)\n- runs.rs wiring: prepare before journal started (refusal -> intent+failed+\n  dispatched=false), delegation family via local_name + first-party origin,\n  execution through execute_prepared; gateway=None keeps R03 path intact\n- review R1 F01 fix: kernel authorize_child_tool_with_registry_id — local_name\n  authoritative for read-only allow/blocklist, registry id depth-defense only;\n  read-class tools reachable for read-only subagents under gateway, write-class\n  blocked on every path incl. ApproveAll; plugin/MCP collision names rejected\n  (InvalidTarget) via server-side origin field; HandleMintFailed dedicated code\n- ownership checker B1 + negative tests N16/N17 (protected executor symbols)\n- acceptance: R04-A03 entry-x-permission matrix, R04-A04 forged credentials\n  PASS via independent reviewers R1(FAIL)/R2(PASS); R03 regression green\n  (10 repair suites pinned, A15/A16); workspace 771 passed / 0 failed\n- evidence: artifacts/rust-tauri/R04/T02-E01; reports under docs/rust-tauri/R04"), "parents": Array [String("fd5fc2c2c583c6f4273ad3fa2122530edd8b152c")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("1a1602c33"), "subject": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R04-T02 route invocations through unified gateway")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790768742), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("fd5fc2c2c583c6f4273ad3fa2122530edd8b152c"), "message": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R04-T01 establish tool contracts and registry\n\n- kernel toolcatalog: ToolTargetId/ToolManifest/ToolRegistry (display name vs\n  authority id, same-name different-origin no-override, aliases resolve to one\n  authority, generation-pinned prepare_invocation with StaleCatalog refusal),\n  schema budget + fail-closed dialect/reference rejection, EffectiveArguments\n  normalization with derived (never model-supplied) summaries\n- ports: ToolRequest carries full effective arguments; ToolOutcome::Success\n  upgraded to structured ToolSuccess (content blocks, resource refs,\n  truncation, run status) for R03 runner + R05 consumption\n- runs.rs anti-forgery gate: digest/arguments mismatch -> trusted digest in\n  journal, failed+dispatched=false, zero dispatch\n- protocol canon: RR-T02-F1 CLOSED (UTF-16 code-unit key order, Rust/TS\n  byte-identical parity incl. non-BMP), RR-T02-F2 closed at T01 consumption\n  point (safe-integer hard fail + PROTOCOL_SPEC section 9 adjudication)\n- review round 1 F01 fix: array minItems/maxItems no longer gated by items\n  subschema (permanent negative regression added, toolcatalog 19/19)\n- acceptance: R04-A01/A02 PASS via independent reviewers R1(FAIL)/R2(PASS);\n  R03 regression suites green (10 repair suites pinned counts, A15/A16)\n- evidence: artifacts/rust-tauri/R04/T01-E01; reports under docs/rust-tauri/R04"), "parents": Array [String("bf6450bcd722668188d1a3091681bf285875ef11")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("fd5fc2c2c"), "subject": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R04-T01 establish tool contracts and registry")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790753381), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("bf6450bcd722668188d1a3091681bf285875ef11"), "message": String("docs(rust-tauri): re-accept R03 after RR2 fixed repair (stage review RR2 PASS)\n\nR03-RR2-F05-01 (requestId normalization inconsistent across memory,\npersistence and restart lookup — the one new RR2 blocker, same family\nas F05) is closed by candidate f4d4b1666: single canonical request-id\nboundary (rule in lingxi-kernel, fact produced once at both admission\nsurfaces), three-state cross-restart binding lookup with Rust-side\nnormalization (no SQLite TRIM), legacy padded cause_ids read-compatible,\nmultiple legacy rows collapsing onto one logical key refused explicitly\nas RequestIdBoundAmbiguous without rewriting frozen lineage.\n\nAcceptance chain: executor failure originals on the unmodified baseline\n(padded foreground retry freshly admitted, run_count=2) → independent\nadversarial review R1 PASS (reviewer's own retest: candidate 3/3 green,\nbaseline c96f7cc6 detached worktree 3/3 red) → candidate committed and\npushed → full verify-stage R03 on f4d4b1666: overall PASS, 15/15\ncommands incl. the seven directed R02 chains, candidateSourceBinding\nstable across all per-command checkpoints, testedShaAtEnd = remote HEAD\n→ fresh stage reviewer RR2 PASS (own retest again 3/3 green vs 3/3 red\non baseline; six-case checklist C01–C06 closed; no R04+ scope creep;\npins only added, never lowered; F01–F08 semantics intact; workspace 73\nsuites / 718 passed / 0 failed).\n\nCloseout: ledger R03-RR2-F05-01 CLOSED_BY_STAGE_REVIEW_RR2 (RR1\nacceptance history preserved), commit receipt with remote confirmation,\nR03_HANDOFF reaccepted_after_rr2_fixed_repair, stage-review report and\ngate evidence under STAGE-REVIEW-RR2/ and RR2-F05-GATE/. Receipt\nreferences the real source commit f4d4b1666; this acceptance commit's\nown SHA is confirmed remotely, not self-referenced in files."), "parents": Array [String("f4d4b16664827010516bc1f5ec6aee5e14b859d3")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("bf6450bcd"), "subject": String("docs(rust-tauri): re-accept R03 after RR2 fixed repair (stage review RR2 PASS)")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790751332), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("f4d4b16664827010516bc1f5ec6aee5e14b859d3"), "message": String("fix(rust-tauri): R03 RR2 repair — canonical request id across admission, lineage and restart lookup (R03-RR2-F05-01)\n\nSingle canonical request-id boundary for the submission surface (RR2\nfixed repair; spec: Lingxi_Rust_Tauri_Taskbooks_2026-09-23/\nLingxi_R03_RR2_2026-09-30/). lingxi-kernel now owns the rule\n(canonical_request_id + REQUEST_CAUSE_ID_PREFIX; Rust trim semantics, no\nSQLite TRIM) and RunLineage::user_submission writes the canonical anchor\nrequest:{canonical}. Both public admission surfaces canonicalize once at\nthe trusted boundary; the same fact flows into the dedup key,\nDriveAuthorization, the durable lineage, the restart lookup and every\nerror echo — the raw id survives only as an audit log field, and a debug\nassertion fences non-canonical drive input. run_store's exact-match\nlookup becomes find_request_binding: LIKE only narrows the scan while\nauthoritative matching normalizes in Rust, so legacy padded cause_ids\nstay linkable, and multiple legacy rows collapsing onto one logical key\nrefuse explicitly (SessionExecuteError::RequestIdBoundAmbiguous, HTTP\n409) without rewriting frozen lineage rows.\n\nNew suite request_id_canonicalization (7 tests, RR2 C01–C05): padded /\nTab / CRLF / Unicode restart retries bind ONE logical request with no\nduplicate external effects; legacy rows linkable or explicitly\nambiguous; namespace isolation and start-failure compensation unchanged\n(existing F05 suites pass unmodified). repair_suites pin table gains the\ntenth suite (RR2-F05, count 7) in the producer script, the xtask mirror\ntable and the stage map note; the nine existing pins are untouched.\n\nEvidence: RR2-F05-E01 (executor; failure originals from the unmodified\nbaseline — the padded foreground retry was admitted as a fresh run,\nrun_count=2) and RR2-F05-R1 (independent adversarial review PASS: the\nreviewer re-ran the padded-restart counterexample on the candidate and\non the c96f7cc6 baseline in a detached worktree, 3/3 green vs 3/3 red;\ncandidate drift-checked by diff sha256). Workspace 73 suites / 718\npassed / 0 failed; fmt/clippy -D warnings/check-contracts/\ncheck-boundaries clean; Cargo.lock unchanged."), "parents": Array [String("c96f7cc635cf18fa83a81b0e28f33d4fed8baf9c")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("f4d4b1666"), "subject": String("fix(rust-tauri): R03 RR2 repair — canonical request id across admission, lineage and restart lookup (R03-RR2-F05-01)")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790744300), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("c96f7cc635cf18fa83a81b0e28f33d4fed8baf9c"), "message": String("docs(rust-tauri): re-accept R03 after adversarial repair (stage review RR1 PASS)\n\nFresh stage reviewer STAGE-REVIEWER-R03-RR1 (no involvement in this\nround's implementation, repair, or workorder reviews) delivers\nSTAGE_VERDICT: PASS on candidate ebcbcad1b9fa1c621b315dd33b58f8a2e01ab9eb:\nthe seven headline counterexamples re-implemented and run against the\nreal service entry and real SQLite (16/16, exit 0), eight adversarial\nvariant spot-checks across seven F-IDs all passing, the original R03\ngate re-run clean in a fresh evidence root (overall PASS, 15/15\ncommands, 17/17 scenarios, 48 leaves = 17 share + 31 deferred, binding\nstable, testedShaAtEnd=ebcbcad1b), fmt/clippy/workspace re-run\n(72 suites / 709 passed / 0 failed), R02 directed chains green with the\nfull-gate red set matching the registered attributions, and the 34-C-ID\nledger closed across all three layers with deferrals intact and no R04\nspillover.\n\nAll eight F01-F08 issues are closed by three-layer evidence (executor\nnormal + adversarial selfchecks, fresh per-workorder independent\nreviews G01-R1..G07-R1, all PASS with red baselines independently\nreproduced). The 2026-09-29 acceptance record and all historical\nevidence remain verbatim; its ruling-2 basis is superseded by this\nround's runtime evidence (FINDING-1 closed by G01, 520bb75b9).\nGovernance residuals (GOV-01/02 seal coordinates, round3\npatch-too-large) remain separately registered, not claimed solved.\nAcceptance record references candidate ebcbcad1b; this commit's own\nSHA is recorded via remote receipt, not written into repo files.\nAllowed next scope restored to the R04 taskbook."), "parents": Array [String("ebcbcad1b9fa1c621b315dd33b58f8a2e01ab9eb")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("c96f7cc63"), "subject": String("docs(rust-tauri): re-accept R03 after adversarial repair (stage review RR1 PASS)")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790741558), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("ebcbcad1b9fa1c621b315dd33b58f8a2e01ab9eb"), "message": String("test(rust-tauri): R03 adversarial repair G07 — counterexamples wired into the formal gate (F08)\n\nThe nine repair suites (59 cases across F01-F07) join verify-stage R03 as\nthe repair_suites command with per-suite exact-count producers, plus the\nR03-RP01 scenario pin; original 16 A-ID scenarios, 14 original commands,\n48 leaves and 7 directed R02 chains are structurally unchanged (verified\nagainst git show 8a6303bcd; stage-map generator regenerated byte-equal).\nA rerunnable gate-negative-test script proves missing leaf / removed\ncommand / removed scenario pin / zero-match filter / missing evidence /\nstale root / mid-run input change each fail loudly and name the gap.\nCurrent reports are corrected additively: R03_REPORT reopen section now\nrecords G01-G06 outcomes and the replacement basis for stage-review\nruling 2 (2026-09-29 STAGE PASS text preserved verbatim); R03_HANDOFF\nmarks FINDING-1 closed by G01 (520bb75b9) and documents the new\ninterfaces (TooLate / AdmissionInFlight / RequestIdBoundToEarlierRun /\nInputTooLarge / full-payload input / background steering); acceptance\nledger gains repair_rounds and R03-RP01 without touching the original 16\nentries. Round deliverables: R03_FIX_NORMAL_SELFCHECK,\nR03_FIX_ADVERSARIAL_SELFCHECK, R03_FIX_ACCEPTANCE_RESULTS (34-C-ID\nred/green/three-layer matrix), R03_FIX_HANDOFF, independent-reviews\nindex.\n\nFull gate on the candidate: verify-stage R03 overall PASS 15/15\ncommands, 17/17 scenarios, 48 leaves = 17 share + 31 deferred, binding\nstable (testedShaAtEnd 8a6303bcd + repair worktree); workspace 72\nsuites/709 passed/0 failed. R02: 7 directed chains green; full\nverify-stage R02 19/20 with the single a16 red attributed (3 registered\nseal-family files = existing GOV-01/02 governance deferrals;\nartifact-core-ustar ENOTEMPTY cleanup race, zero repair-round touches,\nisolated rerun 10/10 green — not folded into old seal categories).\n\nIndependent review R1 PASS (4/4 C-IDs; 59 case names fully matched to\nreal tests; negative script re-run 7/7 refusing; reviewer's own gate\nrerun overall PASS with fresh evidence root; N2 first-run archive shows\nthe gate itself already refused, zero relaxation)."), "parents": Array [String("8a6303bcd477cda891d64fddd6e96fa35017f7ef")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("ebcbcad1b"), "subject": String("test(rust-tauri): R03 adversarial repair G07 — counterexamples wired into the formal gate (F08)")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790734048), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("8a6303bcd477cda891d64fddd6e96fa35017f7ef"), "message": String("fix(rust-tauri): R03 adversarial repair G06 — background steering wired to the authorized inbox (F07)\n\nspawn_background_drive now passes Some(_lease.steering_inbox()) to the\ndetached drive's drive_run call — the same authorized channel the\nforeground path uses (single drain_joined call site in runs.rs). One\nconsumption per next model turn, drained after gate_cancel so a winning\ncancel leaves accepted-but-unconsumed text observable rather than\nconsumed; subagent child runs deliberately keep None (a child draining\nthe parent session inbox would steal user steering; their results\nre-enter via deliver_retained). Bounded inbox capacity and explicit\nSteeringInboxFull rejection are identical across foreground and\nbackground entries; retained text never leaks into an unrelated new run.\n\nIndependent review R1 PASS (4/4 C-IDs re-run; red baseline on 8883923a5\nexit 101 with 7 failures; single-channel and child-None arguments\nverified at source level; 15 protective suites incl. A03/A12 green).\nWorkspace 72 suites/704 passed/0 failed; fmt/clippy clean; Cargo.lock\nunchanged."), "parents": Array [String("8883923a5b30a2a6c0face0c42a9ea143db9a605")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("8a6303bcd"), "subject": String("fix(rust-tauri): R03 adversarial repair G06 — background steering wired to the authorized inbox (F07)")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790728716), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("8883923a5b30a2a6c0face0c42a9ea143db9a605"), "message": String("fix(rust-tauri): R03 adversarial repair G05 — full input payload fidelity, explicit budget refusal (F06)\n\nExecution payload and log summary are now separate: foreground and\nbackground admission pass the full submission input to the run drive\n(chars().take(2000) removed from src/); settle logs record only\ninput_chars/input_bytes counts. One budget, two enforcement legs:\nMAX_SUBMISSION_INPUT_BYTES = DEFAULT_BODY_LIMIT_BYTES (1 MiB) — the same\nnumber and source the HTTP body limit and WS frame limit use — enforced\nat the head of admit_submission, before session read, busy gate, run-id\nallocation, dedup reservation, and any persistent write; over-budget\nsubmissions get a loud 413 input_too_large with zero run rows, zero\nstarted, zero model calls, zero tool dispatch, and no residual G04\nbinding (same-id legal retry admits fresh).\n\nIndependent review R1 PASS (3/3 C-IDs re-run; reviewer redid the red\nbaseline with the final test version on d56e6883d: delivered input\ntruncated to 2000 chars with tail marker cut, and no refusal path\nexisted pre-fix; transport-layer same-budget claim verified at\nlib.rs:3230/ws.rs:441). Workspace 71 suites/696 passed/0 failed;\nfmt/clippy/check-contracts/check-boundaries clean; Cargo.lock unchanged;\nG01-G04 suites green."), "parents": Array [String("d56e6883df1969a05830a3053afabdc693583a62")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("8883923a5"), "subject": String("fix(rust-tauri): R03 adversarial repair G05 — full input payload fidelity, explicit budget refusal (F06)")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790727060), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("d56e6883df1969a05830a3053afabdc693583a62"), "message": String("fix(rust-tauri): R03 adversarial repair G04 — two-phase admission binding, no ghost replay (F05)\n\nSubmissionDedup becomes a staged binding state machine: Pending\nreservation -> Committed (promise point = record_run_started Ok ->\ncommit_durable) -> Unverified on uncertain outcomes. Known\nnever-dispatched failures (bg registry full, spawn window reject,\nforeground persistence failure) revoke the reservation safely; errors\nafter side effects never delete the binding. Replay returns only\nverifiable admissions (Committed with durable row; no DELETE FROM runs\nexists structurally). Unverified entries resolve lazily against the\nreal store (Some->promote / None->revoke / Err->stay). Restart with an\nold key is answered by the explicit persistent anchor\n(run_lineage.cause_id=request:{id}) naming the earlier run — never a\nsilent redo and never a ghost replay.\n\nIndependent review R1 PASS (5/5 C-IDs re-run; red baseline on 198e0da1e\nexit 101 reproducing ghost run id with no durable row; reviewer's\ndynamic WAL-lock probe closed the executor-disclosed no-port gap:\ncandidate compensates on the real chain, old code returns ghost\nreplay). Workspace 69 suites/689 passed/0 failed; fmt/clippy/\ncheck-contracts/check-boundaries clean; Cargo.lock unchanged; G01-G03\nsuites green."), "parents": Array [String("198e0da1e6bd4c3a919982ffe46eb27800dcb78a")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("d56e6883d"), "subject": String("fix(rust-tauri): R03 adversarial repair G04 — two-phase admission binding, no ghost replay (F05)")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790721078), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("198e0da1e6bd4c3a919982ffe46eb27800dcb78a"), "message": String("fix(rust-tauri): R03 adversarial repair G03 — unobserved tool exits classified Unknown (F04)\n\ntool_child.wait() Err(task_exit) no longer fabricates ToolOutcome::Failed:\nunobserved_tool_exit_reason consumes all real TaskExit variants (Panicked\npayload / Aborted / Failed / Completed defensive arm) into a diagnosable\nUnknown reason, preserving idempotency key info and recovery semantics.\nDelegation rejection receipts now carry dispatched=false (verified zero\nchild runs on every SubagentDispatchError path). Trusted negatives kept:\npre-authorization denial stays dispatched=false; genuine external failure\nreceipts stay ConfirmedSettled{Failed}. Startup and repeated recovery\nscans leave Unknown untouched (counter constant across three scans;\nidempotent control case re-verifies with original key only).\n\nIndependent review R1 PASS (4/4 C-IDs re-run; red baseline on ccb09fde6\nexit 101: old code recorded Failed after dispatched panic and\ndispatched=1 on delegation rejection). Workspace 67 suites/673 passed/\n0 failed; fmt/clippy/check-contracts/check-boundaries clean; Cargo.lock\nunchanged; G01/G02 suites green."), "parents": Array [String("ccb09fde679b4cd96e2ba2f5f51e53bce564710f")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("198e0da1e"), "subject": String("fix(rust-tauri): R03 adversarial repair G03 — unobserved tool exits classified Unknown (F04)")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790719112), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("ccb09fde679b4cd96e2ba2f5f51e53bce564710f"), "message": String("fix(rust-tauri): R03 adversarial repair G02 — unified cancel-vs-completion adjudication (F03)\n\nSingle linearization point on RunCancelEntry phase mutex: new Settling\nphase is the irreversible point; claim_terminal adjudicates every\nnon-cancel terminal path (completed all shapes / failed / no-provider\nearly closeout) before finalize's first await via adjudicated_finalize;\natomic fire preserves first reason and monotonic phase (no\nCleaning/Confirmed -> Requested); parent-tree cancellation reflected\neven when child phase lags. CancelRunOutcome::TooLate replaces false\nAccepted; NotLive reload distinguishes AlreadyTerminal vs DanglingActive.\nNine gate_cancel dispatch gates stop new external work after cancel\nacceptance (model/tool loop/intent/authorization/delegation boundaries).\n\nIndependent review R1 PASS (4/4 C-IDs re-run; red baseline reproduced\non 520bb75b9, exit 101: old code completed after Accepted cancel,\nfalse Accepted, double-fired cancels, Started-for-never-dispatched).\nWorkspace 66 suites/666 passed/0 failed; fmt/clippy/check-contracts/\ncheck-boundaries clean; Cargo.lock unchanged; G01 suites green."), "parents": Array [String("520bb75b9906120c78b0d10036577fd911a5a81c")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("ccb09fde6"), "subject": String("fix(rust-tauri): R03 adversarial repair G02 — unified cancel-vs-completion adjudication (F03)")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790716432), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("520bb75b9906120c78b0d10036577fd911a5a81c"), "message": String("fix(rust-tauri): R03 adversarial repair G01 — cancel tree linking (F01) and in-process subagent closeout (F02)\n\nF01: unified link_under entry pairs parent registration with child parent\nref; is_cancelled walks ancestors; registration inherits parent's first\ncancel reason/epoch under the children lock (no-leak protocol); register\nphase starts at Requested when inherited. Real register_linked and\nrun_root_under consumers fixed, not an auxiliary child method.\n\nF02: ChildRun cooperative-cancel window before last-resort drop; PanicGuard\nrecords panics in place; drain_run keeps JoinHandle for detached exit\nobservation (abort request != exit observation); ChildCloseout guarantees\nexactly-once closeout across no-first-poll/drop/panic; accounted ring +\nchild_run_id identity fence stop double-release and stale-callback clears;\nbackground reclaim_finished recycles both registries.\n\nOrdinary parent cancel now closes out in-process: durable cancelled +\nthread busy cleared + active counts (0,0) + supervisor registration empty,\nverified without restart/startup_scan; crash-recovery startup scan tests\nretained green. Independent review R1 PASS (10/10 C-IDs re-run; red\nbaseline reproduced on base code, exit 101). Workspace 65 suites/648\npassed/0 failed; fmt/clippy/check-contracts/check-boundaries clean;\nCargo.lock unchanged."), "parents": Array [String("385ff29409ddbdfd97c4e997cd59860df8d7187f")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("520bb75b9"), "subject": String("fix(rust-tauri): R03 adversarial repair G01 — cancel tree linking (F01) and in-process subagent closeout (F02)")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790716432), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("385ff29409ddbdfd97c4e997cd59860df8d7187f"), "message": String("docs(rust-tauri): reopen R03 pending adversarial repair; register unified issue ledger\n\nAdversarial audit (fix base cd3fb19e6) confirmed F01-F08 (34 C-IDs).\nHistorical STAGE PASS and evidence preserved verbatim; re-acceptance only\nvia this round's fresh independent review. Ledger:\ndocs/rust-tauri/R03/repair-current/R03_FIX_ISSUES.json"), "parents": Array [String("cd3fb19e651f763afc6c75cb3163064fb54ca3fe")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("385ff2940"), "subject": String("docs(rust-tauri): reopen R03 pending adversarial repair; register unified issue ledger")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790692417), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("cd3fb19e651f763afc6c75cb3163064fb54ca3fe"), "message": String("docs(rust-tauri): accept R03 after independent stage review\n\n- STAGE-REVIEWER-R03-R01 (fresh agent, no prior involvement): STAGE_VERDICT\n  PASS on final candidate 1ebb03d9f (stage repair G01 included)\n- independent gate rerun bound to the final commit itself:\n  verify-stage R03 exit 0, testedShaAtEnd=1ebb03d9f, 14/14 commands,\n  16/16 scenarios, 48 leaves (17 stage-share PASS + 31 deferred, 0 fail);\n  six core facts re-executed green (session ordering + cross-session\n  non-blocking / wait-state cancel + subagent permission & propagation /\n  stale attempt + requestId conflict / crash before receipt persist /\n  shutdown rejection / R02 persistence-restart chain); workspace 626/0\n- adjudications: T08 FINDING-1 two-phase closure satisfies A06/T03; G01\n  equivalent assertions tighten (a07) or preserve (a14) protections;\n  a16/E5 residual red decomposed into registered seal-family classified\n  state + NEW governance item (round3 patch replay exceeds git\n  MAX_APPLY_SIZE 1023MiB with a 1.90GB monotonic delta — audit replay\n  scale exhaustion, not an R03 regression) — both deferred to the seal\n  workflow, no allowlist widening\n- R03_HANDOFF: status ACCEPTED with accepted_stage_candidate + governance\n  deferrals; R03_ACCEPTANCE_LEDGER stage_review block; R03_REPORT\n  acceptance section; orchestrator ledger stage ACCEPTED\n- acceptance commit references candidate 1ebb03d9f; its own SHA is\n  registered via the remote receipt, not self-referenced here"), "parents": Array [String("1ebb03d9f89af364a42274efc2cd482f298b1130")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("cd3fb19e6"), "subject": String("docs(rust-tauri): accept R03 after independent stage review")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790690769), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("1ebb03d9f89af364a42274efc2cd482f298b1130"), "message": String("fix(rust-tauri): R03 stage repair G01 — close T08 adjudicated closeout duties\n\n- FINDING-1 (docs only, three stage documents): T06 report's parent-cancel\n  child-run wording corrected per T08 review adjudication with strikethrough\n  traceability (spawn_linked biased-select drops the child drive future:\n  supervision-layer stop holds / A06 valid; durable row settles via the T07\n  startup-scan two-phase closure as interrupted_needs_attention; child's own\n  timeout path still self-settles cancelled); HANDOFF known-gaps entry and\n  R03_REPORT entry annotate the correction without self-closing\n- FINDING-2 equivalent assertion: r02_t04_live_fault_evidence.py restart\n  keyEvents (1,1)->(1,2) plus run state pinned to interrupted_needs_attention,\n  mirroring the already-reviewed T07 in-library fixture change — strictly\n  stronger than the bare count (fabricated completions and blank rows now\n  fail); a07_live_fault_02_check PASS in full gate rerun\n- FINDING-3 equivalent assertion: r02_t07_slow_subscriber.sh storm accepts\n  200 or 409 session_busy retryable (the incumbent Node frozen semantics\n  delivered by R03-T02); a14_slow_subscriber PASS in full gate rerun\n- verification (single-writer chain: F01 edits -> F02 partial -> F03\n  orchestrator-run background matrix, report repairs/R03_STAGE_REPAIR_G01_F01.md):\n  verify-stage R02 19/20 green (was 17/20), only a16 red; verify-stage R03 on\n  the repaired candidate overall PASS 14/14 exit 0 (fresh evidence dir,\n  includes full workspace/fmt/clippy/check-contracts/check-boundaries/A15\n  matrix/A16 seed/7 directed R02 commands)\n- a16 residual red honestly decomposed: registered seal-family classified\n  state PLUS new governance item 'round3 patch replay failed: patch too\n  large' (audit replay machinery scale exhaustion from the monotonic\n  89bc0b64..HEAD delta — NOT an R03 product regression, NOT filed under the\n  old seal-lag class; registered for stage-review adjudication; no allowlist\n  widening, no gate silencing)\n- one environment interference recorded: first full npm test hit two vitest\n  worker-fork crashes (resource contention) making the log unparseable; clean\n  rerun produced parseable shape with file-level coverage + no-new-reds PASS\n\nledger: T08 push receipt backfilled; stage R03 STAGE_REPAIR_DONE_READY_FOR_STAGE_REVIEW"), "parents": Array [String("77bf3bad19e65335269e3f1e7d1dbdbdaba1e259")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("1ebb03d9f"), "subject": String("fix(rust-tauri): R03 stage repair G01 — close T08 adjudicated closeout duties")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790685832), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("77bf3bad19e65335269e3f1e7d1dbdbdaba1e259"), "message": String("feat(rust-tauri): R03-T08 stage gate registration and interface handoff\n\n- xtask: stage_maps/R03.json registered in STAGE_MAPS and pinned in\n  runner_identity (stale-binary detection covers R03.json); 14 commands\n  (full workspace --locked / fmt / clippy / check-contracts /\n  check-boundaries / A15 matrix / A16 seed mechanism / 7 directed R02\n  regression commands), 16 scenarios all REQUIRED, 48 supplemental leaves\n  mirroring the R00 double ledger (17 stage_share_satisfied + 31 deferred,\n  0 fail / 0 blocked); negative probes rerun (unknown stage exit 2, dirty\n  evidence root exit 1); core stage_map/verify/runner_tests changes do not\n  weaken the R02 gate (full verify-stage R02 keeps failing its 3 stale\n  items — honestly reported, not silenced)\n- closes deferred registrations: R02-T04_STORAGE_REGISTRY.json now lists\n  V2/V3/V4 fingerprints (independently recomputed; published V1 byte-\n  identical) and r02_t04_storage_tx.sh S4 decides by registry fingerprint\n  set (full script rerun green); r02_t08_legacy_entry_regression.sh gains\n  an opt-in directed mode (default full semantics unchanged)\n- A15: 12-scenario acceptance matrix through the real service chain\n  (normal / multi-turn / multi-tool / timeout / cancel x2 / duplicate /\n  out-of-order / cross-session / crash recovery / steering / subagent\n  family) with task/call/terminal counts pinned; stubs only emit external\n  responses\n- A16: seed mechanism proven via isolated mutation (seed 0xa16d0000000000\n  captured, replayed twice, removed mutation then same seed + full suite\n  green; honestly labeled mechanism-proof, not a natural discovery); seed\n  override + failure capture added permanently to both property tests\n- handoff docs: R03_REPORT.md / R03_HANDOFF.json / R03_ACCEPTANCE_LEDGER.json\n  with real callable signatures (R04 ToolExecutorPort + journal write order\n  + ask-mode approval-face duty; R05 TurnProviderPort; R07 background\n  submit / cancel / events subscribe), deferred R07 nine leaves intact,\n  no self-referential SHAs\n- review adjudications recorded: FINDING-1 (parent-cancel child-run rows\n  settled by startup scan, A06 supervision holds; T06 wording corrections\n  owed), FINDING-2/3 (R02-era stale assertions a07 keyEvents (1,1)->(1,2)\n  and a14 200-only vs 409 session_busy; equivalent-assertion plans filed\n  as stage closeout duties), E5 seal-family red = audit coordinate lag\n  (governance item, not faked green)\n- R03-T08 PASS (review R1, independent; candidate diff digest 7deab269990f9b43)\n\nverify-stage R03 exit 0; workspace tests green; fmt/clippy/check-contracts/\ncheck-boundaries exit 0; Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock unchanged"), "parents": Array [String("dc42a01e37d1110293ec137402fd3239bd5b7d9d")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("77bf3bad1"), "subject": String("feat(rust-tauri): R03-T08 stage gate registration and interface handoff")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790677817), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("dc42a01e37d1110293ec137402fd3239bd5b7d9d"), "message": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R03-T07 recovery coordinator and shutdown intake gating\n\n- service: recovery.rs RecoveryCoordinator wired into the production\n  bootstrap path (every process start scans non-terminal runs: T05 journal\n  unknown verdicts -> kernel four-state classification -> single\n  commit_run_outcome finalize writes explainable terminal states; no\n  revival of finalized runs; cancelling completes to cancelled; scan\n  failure fail-closed exit 2)\n- kernel: recovery.rs pure classification table (recoverable_wait /\n  retryable_read_only / unknown_side_effect / interrupted_needs_attention,\n  worst-first ladder, user-visible reason + follow-up action per class)\n- A14 shutdown ordering: SubmissionIntake one-way gate closes as the first\n  action of the signal future; rejections happen inside the admission\n  closure (before busy gate / allocation / writes, front and background on\n  the same chain); concurrent submissions during drain all rejected with\n  503 shutting_down retryable over real TCP; same-requestId idempotent\n  replays still answered; existing background runs settle via their own\n  finalize as cancelled; exit 0 with empty residue report\n- A13 crash-point matrix: 11 critical persistence boundaries (run state\n  transitions, journal intent/started/receipt, terminal commit) parked via\n  GatedPort in a real child process, SIGKILL from parent, production-form\n  restart assertions — external counters never re-incremented, interrupted\n  cases have zero final messages (no invented replies), finalize_after\n  keeps completed\n- tests: recovery_crash_points (11 boundaries, seed/pre/post traces),\n  recovery_startup_scan, exit_race_rejections (10+4 concurrent rejections),\n  active_run_listing; T05 A09 and R02-A07 restart assertions re-verified\n  under coordinator semantics (T05 report 10.4 preregistered duty);\n  SERVICE_START_AND_SHUTDOWN.md updated (exit ordering + restart recovery\n  sections, R02 exit-code table untouched)\n- zero new migrations (published V1-V4 fingerprints byte-identical);\n  registry/script sync remains the known T08 item\n- R03-T07 PASS (review R1, independent; candidate diff digest 0e0b2144c141977b)\n\n601 tests / 0 failed (workspace, --locked); fmt/clippy/check-contracts/\ncheck-boundaries exit 0; Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock unchanged"), "parents": Array [String("0c138456bbe791f21621f5a24eb47bc1948f7585")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("dc42a01e3"), "subject": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R03-T07 recovery coordinator and shutdown intake gating")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790673271), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("0c138456bbe791f21621f5a24eb47bc1948f7585"), "message": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R03-T06 subagent lifecycle, background runs, permission inheritance\n\n- kernel: subagent.rs — two-tier permission attenuation (#1616 decay\n  rejection SUBAGENT_WRITE_DENIED_BY_PARENT_READ_ONLY, per-target boundary:\n  full 19-entry blocklist mirror + read-only allowlist + unknown\n  fail-closed); enforced at the T05 journal authorized step in the driver —\n  denied calls never dispatch (dispatched=false receipt + structured\n  Forbidden event; executor stub never consulted)\n- service: subagents.rs — dispatch/reply/close mapped onto the same\n  RunSupervisor::drive_run chain as child runs (linked to parent cancel\n  tree, 10/20 concurrency gates, 30min start-anchored timeout, retained\n  delivery back into session steering); Node semantics traced point-by-\n  point (subagent-tool.ts / subagent-tool-policy.ts / session-permission-\n  mode.ts / experiments/registry.ts, file:line in report §1) with four\n  evidence-backed deviations declared\n- service: background.rs + execute_background_for — same admission chain\n  (busy/dedup) then spawn_detached on the same supervisor (no second\n  scheduler); disconnect semantics defined: client disconnect = continue +\n  reconnect replay, desktop window close = same, service exit = new\n  background drain phase honestly reporting unconfirmed (full policy T07)\n- adapters: migration V4 run_lineage — parentRunId/origin/sourceMessageId/\n  causeId persisted per run, immutable (rewrite = Conflict); published\n  V1/V2/V3 fingerprints byte-identical (registry/script sync deferred to\n  T08 with T04/T05 items)\n- carried fix T03 R1-D1: task_supervisor drain_run deadline branch now\n  saves abort_handle() before timeout so the deadline abort is real;\n  doc/comment/tracing claims corrected; Drop-probe regression added\n  (task_supervisor 7/0, cancellation_tree 8/0 rerun)\n- tests: subagent_permission_inheritance (A11: read-only parent child\n  write denied at real boundary, stub never consulted, negative control\n  passes exactly once, model swap no escalation), subagent_lifecycle,\n  background_disconnect_recovery (A12: continue during disconnect,\n  idempotent replay zero re-execution, queryable, honest exit hook)\n- known advisory deferred to R04: ask-mode parent inheritance collapses\n  to operate under two-tier attenuation (matches isReadOnlyPermissionMode;\n  approval-policy face lands with R04 tool gateway) — recorded for handoff\n- R03-T06 PASS (review R1, independent; candidate diff digest 27010f53cfb3dce8)\n\n580 tests / 0 failed (workspace, --locked); fmt/clippy/check-contracts/\ncheck-boundaries exit 0; Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock unchanged"), "parents": Array [String("6465395cf8e84121ea55b1481afc5711a4d707e8")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("0c138456b"), "subject": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R03-T06 subagent lifecycle, background runs, permission inheritance")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790666173), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("6465395cf8e84121ea55b1481afc5711a4d707e8"), "message": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R03-T05 implement invocation journal and side-effect receipts\n\n- kernel: invocation.rs — InvocationPhase six-state receipt semantics\n  (prepared -> authorized -> started -> succeeded/failed/unknown),\n  InvocationIntent/Receipt/JournalEntry binding owner + run/attempt/\n  generation + target + args digest + idempotency key; recovery decision\n  classify_invocation_recovery (four states + six decisions: safe re-exec /\n  read-only re-exec / same-key idempotent resume / external verify /\n  NeedsAttention no-blind-retry; CONSERVATIVE the only default)\n- adapters: migration V3 invocation_journal (published V1/V2 fingerprints\n  byte-identical; known MINOR: registry/script sync deferred to T08 with\n  T04 F-1, see ledger); StoragePort five journal methods on the single\n  writer queue (ladder validation / idempotent replay / loud conflicts /\n  unknown upgradable by VERIFIED receipts)\n- service: invocations.rs recover_run_invocations (classification +\n  persisted unknown verdicts, idempotent); runs.rs drives real write\n  order: intent and started committed in their own transactions BEFORE\n  external dispatch, receipt committed after external execution and BEFORE\n  stream events\n- tests: A09 — external counter executed once, killed before receipt\n  commit, restart shows counter not auto-incremented + unknown receipt +\n  needs_attention; A10 — idempotent-key stub interrupted before response,\n  resumed with same key: requests=2 executed=1, verified then closed\n  succeeded+dedup_id\n- R03-T05 PASS (review R1, independent; candidate diff digest e78df59386ebe190)\n\n558 tests / 0 failed (workspace, --locked); fmt/clippy/check-contracts/\ncheck-boundaries exit 0; Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock unchanged"), "parents": Array [String("0bf067d9ec329108408f04b00f37f2635fc4a55d")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("6465395cf"), "subject": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R03-T05 implement invocation journal and side-effect receipts")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790661190), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("0bf067d9ec329108408f04b00f37f2635fc4a55d"), "message": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R03-T04 implement late-result fencing and request dedup\n\n- result fence, three layers: port layer async returns carry\n  ResultFence{run_id, attempt, generation}; driver layer verifies identity\n  via fence_verdict BEFORE writing any state (mismatched model result ->\n  audit + loud failure; tool result -> Unknown, never fake success nor\n  blind retry; cancellation wins -> audit + cancelled settlement, content\n  never lands in stream); storage layer record_run_events now rejects all\n  three legs (finalized run / unopened attempt / superseded old attempt —\n  tightened from T01's 'ever opened') and commits stale_result audit rows\n  in an independent transaction so the rejecting rollback cannot swallow\n  them (first-cut flaw caught by own tests and fixed)\n- request dedup (dedup.rs): requestId bound to (owner_kind, owner_subject,\n  session, id) + normalized content digest (CRLF->LF then full sha256);\n  same id + same digest -> idempotent replay of original run; same id +\n  changed digest -> 409 request_id_conflict (no reuse, no new execution);\n  admission completes inside key lock; no-id path byte-identical to before\n- reconnect subscribes only: cursor resume creates zero new runs and zero\n  model calls\n- migration V2 stale_result_audit: versioned additive only; published V1\n  fingerprint untouched (known MINOR F-1: R02-T04_STORAGE_REGISTRY.json and\n  r02_t04_storage_tx.sh S4 not yet synced — forced fix at R03-T08 with R02\n  regression rerun, see ledger)\n- tests: late_result_fence (A07 cross-attempt + cross-run + write-side\n  verification groups), request_dedup (A08 idempotent conflict, runs==1,\n  namespace binding), late_result_fencing_property (real DB, seed\n  0x5eed0000a07df00d, 60 rounds, duplicate/out-of-order/delayed forms,\n  illegal transitions must fail); affected suites adapted with protections\n  preserved\n- R03-T04 PASS (review R1, independent; candidate diff digest 35111570638b82b9)\n\n539 tests / 0 failed (workspace, --locked); fmt/clippy/check-contracts/\ncheck-boundaries exit 0; Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock unchanged"), "parents": Array [String("9e319d64836d5a1656908a81e23ab5edf8370515")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("0bf067d9e"), "subject": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R03-T04 implement late-result fencing and request dedup")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790656462), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("9e319d64836d5a1656908a81e23ab5edf8370515"), "message": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R03-T03 implement cancellation tree and task supervision\n\n- service: cancellation tree (cancel.rs) — CancelScope run-rooted scopes\n  (child model call / approval wait / tool call / child run inherit parent\n  range; eager downward propagation); four-phase CancelPhase (Requested/\n  Cleaning/ConfirmedTerminated/StopUnconfirmed) + honest Abandoned state;\n  CancelRegistry first-fire-wins with bounded queryable verdicts; frozen\n  semantics mapped from Node abortSession / ConfirmStore / STATE_TRANSITIONS R6\n- service: TaskSupervisor (task_supervisor.rs) — spawn_linked biased-select\n  (tree trigger drops child future at await points; cancel wins ties) vs\n  spawn_detached (unrelated background not tree-linked); panics contained\n  as Panicked supervision verdicts; bounded registry with loud rejections\n- cleanup deadline policy: CancelPolicy{cleanup_grace_ms=5000 anchored at\n  fire time, supervised_task_cap=512} + drain_run deadline abort-and-report\n  (StopUnconfirmed recorded in run detail, never claimed quiet; known\n  MINOR D1: deadline-branch abort handle dead code — deferred fix on next\n  touch, see ledger)\n- minimal approval face (approval.rs): production default None (zero\n  behavior change); driver consults before tool exec; Rejected/Aborted\n  execute nothing; late approvals rejected (incumbent ConfirmStore semantics)\n- kernel/adapters: StoragePort::record_run_state_change non-terminal phase\n  transactions (durable cancelling leg + waiting_approval round trip;\n  stored != from loud Conflict)\n- tests: cancellation_tree.rs — A05 parameterized three wait states (queue/\n  approval/stream read: exits wait, cancelled.requested settlement, durable\n  two-phase event order, quotas returned, zero tool executions, late\n  approval rejected); A06 parent cancel stops owned children (incl child\n  run via tree Aborted), unrelated background completes all ticks;\n  non-cooperating tool reaches real StopUnconfirmed\n- R03-T03 PASS (review R1, independent; candidate diff digest 17002eba62e995b2;\n  findings D1/D2 MINOR non-blocking, registered with forced-fix-at-T06)\n\n520 tests / 0 failed (workspace, --locked); fmt/clippy/check-contracts/\ncheck-boundaries exit 0; Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock unchanged"), "parents": Array [String("d075ec8a62bdd9e8346c450b9a4b62668554d9cd")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("9e319d648"), "subject": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R03-T03 implement cancellation tree and task supervision")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790651763), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("d075ec8a62bdd9e8346c450b9a4b62668554d9cd"), "message": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R03-T02 implement session scheduling and limits\n\n- service: SessionSupervisor (session_supervisor.rs) — one RAII owner lease\n  per session, O(1) internal locks never held across model/tool I/O, bounded\n  steering inbox (residual steer carried to next run), registry hard cap\n  with idle eviction\n- service: quota manager (quotas.rs) — model/tool x global/agent/session\n  tiers, fixed acquisition order (no deadlock), FIFO bounded wait queues\n  (full -> loud reject), timeout rejects, RAII release incl.\n  authorization-vs-cancel race return; quota exhaustion settles via single\n  finalize as failed.quota_exhausted.{model,tool}\n- frozen semantics mapped from Node production stack (desktop-session-submit/\n  sessions/chat/session-coordinator, file:line evidence in report §1):\n  busy submit -> 409 session_busy retryable with zero durable side effects;\n  steering drains before each provider turn, Miss->degrade when idle\n- tests: session_serialization.rs (A03 dual-submit trace, A04 cross-session\n  parallel + abort-based permit release with T03 boundary declared),\n  error-path and quota-timeout sisters; 4 fixture updates preserving\n  F01 uniqueness and A09 gapless protections verbatim\n- R03-T02 PASS (review R1, independent; candidate diff digest 7af03d804b5c1736)\n- ledger: T01 push receipt backfilled; env note: tokio test-util feature\n  breaks LAN self-connect case (avoided; feature-free determinism used)\n\n499 tests / 0 failed (workspace, --locked); fmt/clippy/check-contracts/\ncheck-boundaries exit 0; Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock unchanged"), "parents": Array [String("8b2f2cd595625e17b4153af072efc8484b79d5b6")], "refs": Array [], "shortHash": String("d075ec8a6"), "subject": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R03-T02 implement session scheduling and limits")}, Object {"additions": Number(0), "authorName": String("lingxi-dev"), "changedFiles": Number(0), "committedAt": Number(1790646129), "deletions": Number(0), "hash": String("8b2f2cd595625e17b4153af072efc8484b79d5b6"), "message": String("refactor(rust-tauri): R03-T01 implement run and attempt lifecycle\n\n- kernel: finalize decision core (idempotent replay / conflict diagnosis),\n  RunFinish outcome contract (empty_reply, process_only, tool_partial_failure,\n  no_provider_configured, cancelled, interrupted...), attempt/modelcall/toolcall\n  identity helpers; pure transition fn unchanged in authority\n- adapters: commit_run_outcome idempotence tightened to full-settlement\n  equality; record_run_events (late events / unopened attempt -> loud\n  conflict) and record_attempt_started (no revival of finalized runs);\n  no schema migration, Cargo.lock unchanged\n- service: RunSupervisor 